From f5cbe0eb1c0e873df1770487b7771438caf72747 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HempFiend <17104973+jaidenscool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 11:44:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] texture_cache: image_view_memo, skip re-preparing a
 view already prepared this frame

VisitImageView's cached path (TIC entry unchanged, ~98% of calls in Mario Kart World) ran
PrepareImageView every time: view -> image -> flags -> LRU touch, several cache misses per
texture per draw. Each descriptor table index now keeps {view, image state epoch, frame}; while
the view was prepared this frame and no image gained CpuModified/Alias or was deleted since
(g_image_state_epoch, bumped at every such site), the preparation would only touch the LRU with
the same tick again, so it is skipped. Nx2Perf switch image_view_memo (default on); Verify runs
the old path and logs any memo hit that needed preparation (0 in a race).

MKW race: Draw cycles/draw -2.2% (EDEN_NX2_AB in-race A/B, 14M draws); fps pairs off/on
42.6/43.0 and 42.5/45.4. Switch Sports Resort unchanged (59.8 fps).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
